# Top-level dependencies. The workflow installs from requirements.lock, which pins
# every package (including indirect ones) to an exact version and SHA-256 hash, so
# a hijacked or re-uploaded package on PyPI can't slip in. To refresh the lock:
#   uv pip compile forecast/requirements.in --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 \
#     --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 --index-url https://pypi.org/simple \
#     --extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu --index-strategy unsafe-best-match \
#     --exclude-newer <date two weeks ago> -o forecast/requirements.lock
